mastery.solution_text:
$y=2f(2x)$ combines a vertical dilation of factor $2$ with a horizontal dilation of factor $\dfrac12$: $(x,y)\to\left(\dfrac{x}{2},2y\right)$.
$(-1,1)\to(-0.5,2)$ and $(1,-1)\to(0.5,-2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.7,0)--(2.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.7)--(0,3.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-2.3:2.3,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-1.5*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.08:1.08,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{8*\x*\x*\x-6*\x});
\node[gray,right] at (1.6,2.4) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue,right] at (0.55,3.2) {$y=2f(2x)$};
\fill[gray] (-1,1) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[gray] (1,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (-0.5,2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(-0.5,2)$};
\fill (0.5,-2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$(0.5,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
